      "text": "To find the new class mean, we need to calculate the total score of the 36 students and then divide by the total number of students.\n\nFirst, we'll calculate the total score for the 30 students who took the test initially:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total score for 30 students} = 30 \\times 72\\%\n\\]\n\nNext, we'll calculate the total score for the 6 students who took the test on the next day:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total score for 6 students} = 6 \\times 78\\%\n\\]\n\nThen, we'll find the combined total score for all 36 students:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total combined score} = (30 \\times 72\\%) + (6 \\times 78\\%)\n\\]\n\nAnd finally, we'll find the new class mean by dividing the total combined score by the total number of students:\n\n\\[\n\\text{New class mean} = \\frac{\\text{Total combined score}}{36}\n\\]\n\nLet's perform these calculations using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given data\ninitial_students = 30\nfinal_students = 6\n\nmean_score_initial = 72\nmean_score_final = 78\n\n# Total scores for initial and final students\ntotal_score_initial = initial_students * mean_score_initial\ntotal_score_final = final_students * mean_score_final\n\n# Combined total score for all students\ntotal_combined_score = total_score_initial + total_score_final\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = initial_students + final_students\n\n# New class mean\nnew_class_mean = total_combined_score / total_students\nprint(new_class_mean)\n```\n```output\n73.00000000000001\n```\nThe new class mean score for all 36 students, after the tests were taken, is \\(\\boxed{73\\%}\\).",
